WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.227
- The people of Georgia are angry.

00:00:02.227 --> 00:00:03.560
The people of the country are angry.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.840
They're not taking this White House.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.570
We're gonna fight like hell,
I'll tell you right now.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.213
We will stop the steal.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.360
- [Narrator] A week that
began with an extraordinary

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.520
phone call involving baseless
claims of voter fraud,

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.130
escalated to a pro-Trump
riot at the Capitol

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.950
that left five people dead

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.060
and culminated with numerous
administration resignations

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.470
and growing calls for
President Trump's removal

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.750
or resignation.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.111
Here's a look at how the
historic week unfolded.

00:00:31.111 --> 00:00:32.692
- [Donald] I won this election by hundreds

00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:33.525
of thousands of votes.

00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:35.520
There's no way I lost Georgia.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.110
- [Narrator] In a Saturday
phone call President Trump urged

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.500
Georgia Secretary of
State, Brad Raffensperger,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.757
to overturn the state's
November election results.

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:45.260
- [Donald] All I want to do is this:

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:50.260
I just want to find 11,780 votes,

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.850
which is one more than we have,

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:59.130
because we won the state
and flipping the state

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.730
is a great testament to our country.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.520
- [Narrator] Raffensperger
and his general counsel

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.800
pushed back on the unfounded claims.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.380
- [Brad] Well, Mr. President,
the challenge that you have

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.170
is the data you have is wrong.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.970
- [Narrator] But President
Trump continued to double down.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.450
- There's no way we lost
Georgia, there's no way.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.580
That was a rigged election,

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.850
but we're still fighting it,

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.150
and you'll see what's going to happen.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.200
We'll talk about it.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.807
- [Narrator] At a Monday
rally ahead of Georgia's

00:01:25.807 --> 00:01:27.330
Senate runoff elections,
the President repeated

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.200
the unfounded allegations and said

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.620
that Vice President Mike Pence

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.180
had the power to reject
electoral college votes

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.303
at a joint session of
Congress later that week.

00:01:36.303 --> 00:01:38.343
- I hope that our great Vice President,

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.480
our great Vice President
comes through for us.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.643
He's a great guy.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.820
Plus, if he doesn't come through,

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.810
I won't like him quite as much.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.630
- [Narrator] The pressure
play put the Vice President

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.960
in the spotlight, even
though legal experts said

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.320
he didn't have the authority
to reject state results.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.170
- The future of the
country is on the ballot

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.502
here in Georgia today.

00:02:00.502 --> 00:02:02.870
- Georgia voters have never had more power

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.730
than you have today.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.230
- [Narrator] On Tuesday, as
Georgia voters went to the polls

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.620
to decide which party
would control the Senate,

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.720
the President tweeted and
retweeted claims of voter fraud,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.240
which were flagged by Twitter as disputed.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.230
- Democrat Raphael Warnock will unseat

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.930
Republican Senator Kelly Loeffler.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.820
- Democrat Jon Ossoff will defeat

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.480
the Republican David Purdue.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.390
- And both of those
Senate seats are flipping.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.420
- This is at the feet of Donald J. Trump.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.180
He basically saved
Chuck Schumer's chances.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.720
- [Narrator] The victories gave Democrats

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.453
full control of Washington.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.330
On Wednesday, President Trump promoted

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.400
and attended a save
America rally in Washington

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.770
that took place just
before Congress convened

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:47.340
to certify President-elect
Joe Biden's victory

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.210
in the November election.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.550
- This is Donald Trump's Republican party.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.870
- Let's have trial by combat.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.900
- [Narrator] The rally
concluded with President Trump

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.070
encouraging his supporters
to March to the Capitol.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.990
- We're going to walk
down Pennsylvania Avenue.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.950
I love Pennsylvania Avenue.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:07.560
And we're going to the Capitol.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.520
We're going to try and
give our Republicans,

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.420
the weak ones, because the strong ones

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.270
don't need any of our help.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.466
We're going to try and
give them the kind of pride

00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:23.040
and boldness that they need
to take back our country.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.440
- [Narrator] In the hours that followed,

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.730
rioters wearing pro-Trump
gear attacked police officers,

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.740
smashed windows and broke
into the Capitol building,

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.620
forcing lawmakers to seek cover

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.150
and temporarily halting
the democratic process

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.870
of certifying the electoral college votes.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.440
Five people, including a
Capitol police officer,

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.623
died as a result of the unrest.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.470
That afternoon, President Trump

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.400
posted a video on social media.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.090
- It was a landslide election,
and everyone knows it,

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.540
especially the other side,

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.560
but you have to go home now.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.200
We have to have peace.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.560
- [Narrator] Some social media companies

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.740
removed the video and later
locked the President's accounts

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.900
citing violations of their policies.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.700
- Criminal behavior will never dominate

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.050
the United States Congress.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.413
This institution is resilient.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.913
Our democratic republic is strong.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:22.790
The American people deserve nothing less.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.970
- [Narrator] Wednesday night
after the Capitol was clear,

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:28.260
Congress reconvened to
finish certifying the votes

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.270
and back in session, some Republicans

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.170
who had planned to object
to the certification,

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.630
had a change of heart.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.340
- The events that have transpired today

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.340
have forced me to reconsider.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.060
And I cannot now in good conscience

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:43.240
object to the certification
of these electors.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.990
- The votes for president
of the United States

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.810
are as follows:

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.300
Joseph R Biden Jr. of
the state of Delaware

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.950
has received 306 votes.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.360
Donald J. Trump of the state of Florida

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.380
has received 232 votes

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.560
- [Narrator] On Thursday,
several government officials

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.160
resigned, top democratic lawmakers called

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.750
for President Trump's removal,

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.350
and President-elect Biden
blamed President Trump

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.220
for Wednesday's events,
condemning the violence

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.670
- What we witnessed
yesterday was not descent.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.810
It was not disorder.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.810
It was not protest.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.283
It was chaos.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.600
They weren't protesters.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.810
Don't dare call them protests.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:29.670
They were a rightist
mob, insurrectionists,

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.320
domestic terrorists.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.090
- [Narrator] Thursday
evening, President Trump

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.730
posted a new video online
addressing the nation.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:39.450
- A new administration will be
inaugurated on January 20th.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.380
My focus now turns to ensuring a smooth,

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.382
orderly and seamless transition of power.

00:05:45.382 --> 00:05:49.780
This moment calls for
healing and reconciliation.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.660
- [Narrator] He called the
storming of the U S Capitol

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.490
by a mob of his supporters,
a heinous attack,

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.740
but accepted no
responsibility for the riot.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.190
Friday morning, President
Trump announced on Twitter

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.280
that he would not be
going to the inauguration

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.090
of President-elect Biden on January 20th.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.210
By the afternoon, Democrats had drafted

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.990
an article of impeachment that they plan

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:10.360
to introduce Monday.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.440
The White House pushed
back against the effort,

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:13.867
and in a statement said,

00:06:13.867 --> 00:06:15.717
"A politically motivated impeachment

00:06:15.717 --> 00:06:18.427
"against a president with 12
days remaining in his term

00:06:18.427 --> 00:06:21.650
"will only serve to further
divide our great country".

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.440
Friday evening, Twitter
said it permanently banned

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.900
President Trump's Twitter account,

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:29.070
due to the risk of further
incitement of violence.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.920
A tweet from president Trump's official

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:33.160
US government account
said Twitter employees

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.440
had coordinated with Democrats to try

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.690
and silence himself and his followers,

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.210
adding, "we will not be silenced".

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.210
Twitter removed the
tweets from its platform,

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.160
citing a policy violation.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.200
Into the weekend, authorities
continued to make arrests

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.380
and seek information
about the perpetrators

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.763
of Wednesday's riot.

